      "content": "6.1 Indian Constitution — Key Articles for Exams"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Key Articles of the Indian Constitution form the backbone of polity questions in competitive exams.",
        "The Karnataka State Legislature is responsible for enacting state-level legislation and policies.",
        "The Karnataka High Court serves as the highest judicial authority within the state.",
        "Karnataka Lokayukta acts as an independent anti-corruption agency to ensure administrative integrity.",
        "Panchayati Raj in Karnataka establishes rural local self-governance and grassroots administration."
      ],
